---
/**
 * Privacy Statement — /privacy
 * UI chrome matches https://www.ebcflex.com/privacystatement/
 * Copy is original paraphrase (not a verbatim reprint of the source legal text).
 */
import EbcMarketingLegal from "../layouts/ebc-marketing-legal.astro"
import { SITE_DISPLAY_NAME } from "@/lib/site-url"

const pageTitle = `Privacy statement and data practices | ${SITE_DISPLAY_NAME}`
const pageDescription =
  "How Employee Benefits Corporation collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information for FSA, HSA, HRA, LSA, COBRA, and related participant services."
---

<EbcMarketingLegal
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  pageName="Privacy Statement"
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <h1>Our Privacy Statement</h1>
  <hr class="ebc-legal-rule" />
  <p class="legal-lede">
    This Privacy Statement explains information Employee Benefits Corporation (“EBC”, “we,” “our,”
    “us”) collects and uses to deliver products and services. Those offerings include flexible spending
    accounts, health reimbursement arrangements, health savings accounts, lifestyle spending accounts,
    COBRA administration, and other employer-sponsored programs (each an “Account,” together the
    “Services”).
  </p>
  <p>
    We may revise this statement at any time. Review it regularly. Using the Services, website, or
    mobile application means you accept this Privacy Statement. If you do not agree, do not use those
    channels. This statement, the website, and the mobile application are intended for people who live
    in the United States.
  </p>
  <p>
    This statement does not cover third-party websites or apps that link to or from our sites, or sites
    that publish their own privacy notices. Our digital properties are not directed to children under
    13, and we do not knowingly solicit online data from, or market online to, children under 13.
  </p>

  <h2>Personal Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>To provide Services, we may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name, email, and physical address</li>
    <li>Social Security Number (SSN) and date of birth</li>
    <li>Phone number</li>
    <li>Identifying information for dependents</li>
    <li>Identifying information for people you authorize to use or view Account information</li>
    <li>
      Account activity such as elections, balances, payment history, claims, reimbursements,
      distributions, and contributions
    </li>
    <li>Banking and payment information</li>
    <li>
      Employer-provided data needed for annual cafeteria plan nondiscrimination testing, including
      contribution amounts, compensation details, and ownership or officer status
    </li>
    <li>Information described in the Cookies section below</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How We Collect Your Personal Information</h2>
  <p>
    We collect personal information directly from you through the website, mobile application, or other
    forms, and indirectly from your employer, insurance company, or affiliates when needed to run the
    Services.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and Website Tracking</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies and analytics tools help us deliver services, answer inquiries, fix online issues, improve
    the site and experience, and measure quality programs. We may share this technical data with
    vendors that process it for those purposes. It typically does not reveal your name, contact details,
    or claim content, but may include IP address, browser and device traits, OS, language, referring
    URLs, device name, country, location, and how or when you use the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not sell this information for marketing. Security controls and vendor agreements help protect
    privacy. Related cookie choices are also described in the
    <a href="/disclosures">Terms of Use</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Log Files</h2>
  <p>
    IP addresses support website administration and are not linked to personally identifiable
    information in that use. Limited non-identifying device and OS data may support mobile application
    troubleshooting.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Use and Share Personal Information</h2>
  <p>We may use or share personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Authenticate identity and open, maintain, and administer Accounts</li>
    <li>Process and pay benefit claims</li>
    <li>Communicate about Services or Accounts</li>
    <li>Make Pay Your Provider payments</li>
    <li>Help prevent fraud, security incidents, and financial loss</li>
    <li>Respond to information you request</li>
    <li>Engage service providers that help deliver Services</li>
    <li>Record transactions and communications</li>
    <li>Meet legal, regulatory, administrative, or subpoena requirements</li>
    <li>Follow your authorization or instructions</li>
    <li>Otherwise lawfully operate the business, provide Services, or administer Accounts</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell or rent personal information. We also do not “share” personal information as that
    term is used under California law for cross-context behavioral advertising. Sharing is limited to
    what this statement describes and what law permits.
  </p>
  <p>
    Access is limited to employees, affiliates, and service providers who need the information to
    deliver Services, fight fraud or security incidents, or run the business lawfully. For
    employment-based Accounts, we may disclose Account details — such as type, balance, activity, and
    contributions — to a current or former employer. If you authorize family members or others, you are
    responsible for their Account actions; authorized users may see balances after standard
    authentication.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, Account type, and data category, you may have rights to know, access,
    update, or remove personal information. Deletion requests often require coordination with a current
    or former employer when data relates to an employer benefit plan. We typically cannot delete that
    information unless the employer authorizes it. You may also update some details in your online
    account or by emailing
    <a href="mailto:participantservices@ebcflex.com">participantservices@ebcflex.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Rights of California Residents</h2>
  <p>
    Employee Benefits Corporation acts as a service provider under California privacy laws when it
    collects personal information for employers that administer employee benefit plans. Deletion
    generally requires an employer or former employer instruction. Personal information is not disclosed
    to third parties for their direct marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Information Security</h2>
  <p>
    Physical, administrative, and technical safeguards protect personal information against unauthorized
    use or disclosure. Electronic channels cannot be guaranteed completely secure — for example,
    transmissions over the internet may be intercepted. Protect your Account with a strong, unique
    password and keep that password confidential.
  </p>

  <h2>Email Communications</h2>
  <p>
    Email is used for Account transactions, service updates, education, and related notices. Service
    emails typically cannot be opted out of. Marketing emails may include unsubscribe links.
  </p>

  <h2>Push Notifications</h2>
  <p>
    The mobile application may send push notifications about activity such as transaction confirmations,
    claim updates, or alerts. Sensitive Account details are not placed in notification content. Manage
    or disable notifications in device settings. Secure vendors may process limited device identifiers
    solely to deliver notifications. Delivery and response metrics may be used to improve services and
    are not used for unrelated purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>Applications for Employment with Employee Benefits Corporation</h2>
  <p>
    Candidate information — such as resumes, work history, and references — may be collected for open
    roles and used to match skills, experience, and education to positions.
  </p>

  <h2>Gramm-Leach-Bliley Notice</h2>
  <p>
    A separate Gramm-Leach-Bliley privacy notice describes how nonpublic personal financial information
    is collected, shared, and protected. Review that notice relating to personal financial information
    for additional detail.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Information</h2>
  <p>Questions about this Privacy Statement can be sent to EBC:</p>
